  "schema": "parserstudio.generic-differential-seeds.v1",
  "purpose": "Seed lines for the browser versus generated-Ruby differential of Generic Structural (scripts/verification/semantic-oracle.ts differential). Every seed is a line from the fixtures and tests of this repository and tests that the browser extractor parses; the two shortest per result mode. The oracle derives the variants (PRI, VERSION, month, host and key mutations, Unicode white space and separators, control characters, impossible dates, time zones and fractions of a second, JSON escapes, comments and nesting, CSV quoting, and a fixed pseudo-random stream of token insertions, deletions and splices) and requires the same decision and the same field tree from both engines for every variant. No expected value is stored here: the two engines are the reference for each other, and the hand-authored goldens (semantic-goldens.v1.json) say which of them is right.",
